>> title: Jerk Marinade
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: jamaican, chiles, allspice, marinade, chicken
>> counters: Smokehouse, Meat and Three
>> aka: jerk seasoning, jerk paste, Jamaican jerk
>> pairs-with: coconut-rice
>> servings: 6
>> time: 15 min
>> step.1: blend to a coarse paste
>> step.2: blend in
>> step.3: blend smooth
>> step.4: blend in, marinate overnight

Blend @scallions{6}(trimmed and cut up), @Scotch bonnet chiles{4}(stemmed; seeded for less heat), @garlic{6%cloves}, @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(chopped), and @fresh thyme leaves{2%Tbs} to a coarse paste in a #blender{}.

Add @ground allspice{2%Tbs}, @freshly grated nutmeg{1/2%tsp}, @dark brown sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g), and @kosher salt{1%Tbs} to @&(~1)paste{} and blend again.

Pour @soy sauce{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and @lime juice{1/4%cup}(60 mL) into @&(~1)paste{} and blend smooth.

Blend @vegetable oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL) into @&(~1)marinade{} until it looks glossy, then rub it into 4 lb of chicken and chill it overnight.
